  "description": {
    "format": "nuke_help_html",
    "plain_text": "You can load audio files into Nuke much in the same way as images using the AudioRead node. You can read in uncompressed WAV and AIFF files, and flipbook them with your footage for playback. In addition you can display an audio waveform for your audio clip in the Curve Editor and Dope Sheet and access its animation curve through expressions.",
    "source": "nuke.Node.help()",
    "text": "You can load audio files into Nuke much in the same way as images using the\nAudioRead node. You can read in uncompressed WAV and AIFF files, and flipbook\nthem with your footage for playback. In addition you can display an audio\nwaveform for your audio clip in the Curve Editor and Dope Sheet and access its\nanimation curve through expressions."
  },
